<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalmar Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1397–1523</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a> Union was the personal union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under a single monarch, created through the work of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a> and sealed by the coronation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a> at Kalmar in 1397. Danish dominance provoked repeated Swedish revolts and long periods of rule by Swedish regents, and the union broke apart when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a> was elected King of Sweden in 1523.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalmar-union.jpg" alt="Kalmar Union" width="320" height="298" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ssolbergj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalmar_Union_ca._1400.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
